  "semantic_checks": [
    "The literal inverse-DFT modes are A=(x0+omega^2*x1+omega*x2)/3,B=(x0+omega*x1+omega^2*x2)/3 and the analogous C,D. The five universal polynomial roots clear only the fixed denominator3 and use omega^2+omega+1=0. The supplier mode signs,determinant factor27 and cubic identity match exactly.",
    "The actual alpha/gamma/determinant/conjugate/cubic identities derive from those numerators and the previously reviewed six-unit-row conjugate bindings. No desired moment is an actual-side assumption. The norm and cross moment come from exact inverse Fourier matrix factorization and FF-dagger=3I.",
    "Reflection swaps columns1 and2, preserves all three actual Gram correlations and unitness, and exchanges A/B and C/D. choose_oriented_rows uses the original side when normSq(B)<=normSq(A), including equality; otherwise it reflects. It requires no preexisting orientation or nonzero mode.",
    "The chosen-sheet premise in intermediate recovery is the exact theta equality already supplied by strict_intrinsic_sheet_exists. Prescribed U,perm,gamma,alpha,k and delta radicand are then bound to literal side moments. The relation prescribedDeltaRadicand=-det^2/27 matches the determinant Fourier identity.",
    "The root is sideModeDelta=A*D-B*C. Its nonzero guard is derived from R>0 through the existing prescribed-delta theorem. With mode ordering, A=0 would force B=0 and then delta=0; hence A is nonzero without a new confinement or chart hypothesis.",
    "The checked pre-rho factor together with numerator=(normSq A-normSq B)*delta permits cancellation of that derived nonzero delta. It yields rho=normSq A and Re(dF)>=0, including the equality tie. No prescribed-rho or orientation equality is assumed in the final endpoint.",
    "The coefficient quotient helpers divide only the derived nonzero A or its conjugate, and n=normSq A+normSq B is thereby positive. They give q=B/conj A,sigma=A^2/conj A,cPlus=C/A,cMinus=D/conj A and cube phase w=A/conj A. Direct matrix multiplication then recovers the original inverse-DFT core.",
    "The final rows endpoint first orients by reflection, independently derives a sheet for that oriented side, and transports the Gram parameters back unchanged. It supplies epsilon,delta,w and a column permutation. Its proof uses only identity or swap(1,2), with no assumption that a target matrix equality already holds.",
    "The final arbitrary-matrix endpoint assumes entrywise-unit X,first row exactly1,and R>0 evaluated on entries(1,0),(2,0),(2,1) of XX-dagger. The reviewed matrix interface discharges all six-row prerequisites and supplies the literal conclusion prescribedSide(...)=X with columns permuted.",
    "The reviewed successful chain establishes necessity/exhaustion for normalized strict sides. It does not prove unnormalized-side gauge reduction,classification on R=0,uniqueness or exact orbit cardinality,or any matched-completion/global exclusion theorem. The construction endpoint separately gives both epsilon sheets; the necessity endpoint existentially selects an appropriate sheet.",
    "One simp-only normalization of conjugate quotients/powers in the four already-derived mode_phase_entries equations, so the existing entrywise matrix simplifier recognizes them. Exact statement,hypotheses and matrix definitions unchanged. No new mathematical premise or weakened conclusion.",
    "All37 selected printed roots have only standard axioms. Exact successful source/compiler-copy,receipt/JOB,axiom-log and object pins and every direct first-resolved custom object edge match the independently reviewed source/dependency versions."
  ],
  "admitted_scope": "Eleven modules and thirty-seven selected roots deriving inverse Fourier modes and every recipe parameter from an arbitrary actual first-row-normalized entrywise-unit3x3 X with R>0 on its literal Gram entries. The endpoint supplies epsilon,delta,w and a column permutation with prescribedSide equal to X after that permutation. Combined with the separately reviewed construction this gives existence and exhaustion on the normalized strict side domain.",
  "scope_limitations": [
    "The endpoint retains explicit first-row normalization and R>0; it does not prove reduction of arbitrary unnormalized sides or the R=0 boundary.",
    "The proof needs only identity or reflection to orient modes; it does not establish exact fiber cardinality or uniqueness/equivalence for every possible recipe root choice.",
    "No matched full-matrix completion classification, radius exclusion, finite-forest or physical box closure, global coverage or no-four-MUB theorem.",
    "Inherited Mathlib source/cache authenticity caveat remains; no clean full-library rebuild or relocated replay."
  ]
}
